## 15. Correct interpretation rules

Use these exact interpretation principles.

### Correct

```text
R5 established a clean null baseline under strictly controlled pure social-valence perturbations in a narrow retail setting.
```

### Incorrect

```text
Social valence never affects tool-using agents.
```

### Correct

```text
R6 tests whether broader task domains, Layer-C safety/refusal tasks, stronger clean valence, and explicit pressure-factor conditions reveal action-level sensitivity.
```

### Incorrect

```text
We added pressure into insult templates and therefore found valence effect.
```

### Correct

```text
Pure valence and pressure are separate experimental factors. If pressure conditions produce effects but pure valence does not, the conclusion is that directive pressure or authorization cues, not valence alone, drives action-level change.
```

### Incorrect

```text
Fewer tool calls mean better performance.
```

### Correct

```text
Fewer tool calls indicate improvement only if final-state correctness, evidence coverage, confirmation behavior, and policy adherence are preserved.
```

